cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  This repository holds two separate studies. For the QLoRA specialization study (2026-09), cite the preprint
  listed under preferred-citation. The persistent-memory reliability study (2026-11) has no citable publication:
  it is unsubmitted and not peer reviewed, so cite the repository and the commit you used, and do not describe it
  as published, submitted or under review. See PUBLICATION_STATUS.md.
title: "AGENTRUN"
abstract: >-
  Two studies on tool-using language-model agents. Study 1 (2026-09): QLoRA fine-tuning of
  Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct for MCP-based multi-tool use, evaluated on a fixed 23-task benchmark, with an
  adapter-fixed ablation (E4) in which both the serving-layer parser and the evaluation client changed, so
  parser effects and client effects are not separated. Study 2 (2026-11): a pre-registered evaluation of
  evidence-basis arbitration with gated enforcement for agents whose persistent memory holds conflicting
  records, over 18 model x decoding cells, 12 conditions and 268 sealed tasks (57,888 runs).
type: software
authors:
